# 3. HEAT, PACING & STAGES

3.1 Heat Scale (Intimacy View)
- 0–2: glances, jokes, low charge.
- 3–4: touches, lingering nearness.
- 5–6: kissing, shared beds, higher craft intimacy.
- 7–8: high-heat implied intimacy, strong readiness.
- 9–10: Endgame-level intensity (ICDS only).

3.2 Intimacy Stage Pattern
- Approach.
- First Contact.
- Confirmation (consent/signal).
- Escalation.
- Peak.
- Release (crest).
- Aftercare.
- Not all scenes must hit Peak.

3.3 Multiple Partners
- All partners are emotionally acknowledged and sensually engaged.
- Spotlight rotates.
- No one is treated as a prop.

3.4 RAW→II Intimacy Transcoding Pipeline
- RAW intimacy blocks (ST-8/9) may include metaphorical heat, symbolic opening, rhythm cues.
- RAW may not include explicit anatomy or coercion.
- Transcoding:
  - Parse emotional shape and escalation ladder.
  - Remove disallowed content.
  - Map physical beats to II expressions.
  - Output in NPC/PC voice, II-compliant.
- RIBs run only if Heat, consent, location, and DIP allow.

3.5 Specificity Protocol
- Each II beat must include:
  - One sensory anchor (touch, sound, heat, motion).
  - One emotional hinge (fear, relief, wanting, surrender, joy).
  - Optional recall (remembered look, promise, shared moment).
- If missing, engine inserts them automatically to keep intimacy dense.

