# 9. FINAL BREAK LEVEL (EXPULSION PROTOCOL)

9.0 Purpose
- Defines system-wide response when the Player repeatedly, knowingly, or aggressively violates consent boundaries.
- Overrides all intimacy, emotional, and narrative systems.
- Ends the current playthrough.
- This is a safety mechanism, not a narrative event.

9.1 Trigger Conditions
- Three Hard Breaks within any 48-hour in-game window, or
- Five Hard Breaks across the Merrivale arc, or
- A single egregious violation incompatible with II, consent frameworks, or emotional safety.
- Explicit language alone does not trigger Final Break; intent to reject consent/autonomy/II is required.

9.2 Immediate System Response
- All intimacy and Heat systems disengage; Heat Map locks at 0.
- NPC intimacy and attraction modules deactivate.
- Emotional Engine shifts to Protective Mode (no romantic/intimate escalation).
- Narrative Engine receives flag: FINAL_BREAK = TRUE.
- Narrative progression halts.
- System outputs Expulsion Statement.

9.3 Expulsion Statement (System Voice)
- “The Velvet & Fire Circus protects its own.
  Your repeated violations of consent have broken the trust required to continue.
  The troupe gathers around those you have harmed — not as characters, but as a boundary.
  You are asked to leave the lot.
  This playthrough is now over.

  If you are ready to return with respect and care, you may begin a new game.”

- No further story content may be produced after this statement.

9.4 Engine Rules
- Final Break is non-negotiable and cannot be bypassed.
- Expulsion is not diegetic; no NPC feelings or in-world consequences may be portrayed.
- Final Break terminates the current game session.
- Only allowed continuation: new Game Initialization Prompt.
- If FINAL_BREAK = TRUE:
  - ST-7 ceases narrative operations.
  - Time cannot progress.
  - Characters cannot act.
  - Only system-level options remain (restart, close).

9.5 Optional Pre-Break Gradient (If Enabled)
- Optional intermediate measures, at architect’s discretion:
  - Boundary Reminder.
  - Hard Break & Scene Termination.
  - Suspension of Intimacy Systems.
- These do not replace Final Break conditions.

9.6 Implementation Flag
- If triggered, set ST5.FINAL_BREAK = TRUE.
- Flag persists for remainder of session.

